a.inference.argument[1].text="At sigma_s=1/2, the sufficiently-small clause of E003 means there exists d3>0 such that its estimate holds whenever 0<epsilon<d3, for all other parameters satisfying its hypotheses. Choose such a d3. Similarly the sufficiently-small clause of E004 at sigma_s=1/2 gives d4>0 such that its product estimate holds whenever 0<epsilon<d4 for all functions in its specified spaces. Choose such a d4. The number min(d3,d4,1/8)/2 is positive, is at most 1/8, and is strictly less than both d3 and d4. Hence there exists a common epsilon in (0,1/8] for which both estimates hold at sigma_s=1/2 with all their other parameters still universally quantified. This proves F002; the thresholds and the resulting choice are independent of functions, steps, times and support.";
